ed**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Only the first auxiliary moves; the participle stays after they.","B":"Has does not agree with they.","C":"Move the first auxiliary **have** before they; keep the participle after the subject.","D":"This is ordinary statement order rather than the requested inversion."}}},{"id":"761e6c71-70bc-56c1-a6c0-4948d9fa4678","topicSlug":"inversion","level":"C1","prompt":"Replace “If we had measured the garden fence”: “____ the garden fence, we would have finished earlier.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"If had we measured"},{"id":"B","text":"We had measured"},{"id":"C","text":"Had we measuring"},{"id":"D","text":"Had we measured"}],"answerId":"D","hint":"A formal unreal past condition can begin **Had + subject + participle**.","explanation":"Omit if and invert **had we** to express the unreal past condition.","keywords":["inverted-past-condition"],"skill":"inverted-past-condition","contextKey":"inversion-3","fingerprint":"50e55afe64931eed97da23f314ab30612bb9a4cae9d618e0ac543a6273e4c507","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-inversion"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["A formal unreal past condition can begin **Had + subject + participle**.","Omit if and invert **had we** to express the unreal past condition.","Choose **Had we measured**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Do not combine if with this inverted conditional structure.","B":"Without if or inversion, this would not mark the requested conditional relationship.","C":"Had requires a past participle, not -ing.","D":"Omit if and invert **had we** to express the unreal past condition."}}},{"id":"66fd2ae2-ff30-5924-a6f9-d8338726ff4b","topicSlug":"inversion","level":"C1","prompt":"Use inversion in the main clause: “Only after the call ____ the garden fence.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"did she measure"},{"id":"B","text":"she measured"},{"id":"C","text":"did she measured"},{"id":"D","text":"she did measure"}],"answerId":"A","hint":"The inversion belongs in the **main clause following only after**.","explanation":"Only after the call is a limiting opening; invert **did she** and use base measure.","keywords":["only-after-scope"],"skill":"only-after-scope","contextKey":"inversion-3","fingerprint":"90c69c698401247bef69fa3d73388239e219208544072825b9bde6c2c04bfaa2","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-inversion"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["The inversion belongs in the **main clause following only after**.","Only after the call is a limiting opening; invert **did she** and use base measure.","Choose **did she measure**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Only after the call is a limiting opening; invert **did she** and use base measure.","B":"The requested formal main clause needs inversion after this limiting opening.","C":"Did already marks the past, so the next verb must be base.","D":"The auxiliary must precede the subject in the inverted main clause."}}},{"id":"8ff1a959-3281-5e0d-a37c-ea0eb2e839ec","topicSlug":"inversion","level":"C1","prompt":"Use formal inversion: “Rarely ____ the travel leaflet without help.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"does she translate"},{"id":"B","text":"she translates"},{"id":"C","text":"does she translates"},{"id":"D","text":"she does translate"}],"answerId":"A","hint":"A fronted negative-frequency expression triggers **auxiliary before subject**.","explanation":"Fronted **rarely** triggers **does she + translate**; does carries present agreement.","keywords":["negative-fronting-present"],"skill":"negative-fronting-present","contextKey":"inversion-4","fingerprint":"8ee1d8df1a29e4b98b9ea44bf7562d3f0e7e3208b5a6975492bec3db9e7af970","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-inversion"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["A fronted negative-frequency expression triggers **auxiliary before subject**.","Fronted **rarely** triggers **does she + translate**; does carries present agreement.","Choose **does she translate**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Fronted **rarely** triggers **does she + translate**; does carries present agreement.","B":"This retains ordinary statement order instead of the requested inversion.","C":"Does carries agreement, so the main verb must lose -s.","D":"The auxiliary must precede the subject after fronted rarely."}}},{"id":"db2ad5c0-a1cf-5929-aca0-53b5f6d930c4","topicSlug":"inversion","level":"C1","prompt":"Use formal inversion: “Never ____ the travel leaflet so quickly.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"has they translated"},{"id":"B","text":"have they translated"},{"id":"C","text":"they have translated"},{"id":"D","text":"have translated they"}],"answerId":"B","hint":"Move **only have** in this perfect construction.","explanation":"Move the first auxiliary **have** before they; keep the participle after the subject.","keywords":["negative-fronting-perfect"],"skill":"negative-fronting-perfect","contextKey":"inversion-4","fingerprint":"8f77995500713413d6d619ed873f1f762495b3020f991d4cbd148ebad408b8bd","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-inversion"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Move **only have** in this perfect construction.","Move the first auxiliary **have** before they; keep the participle after the subject.","Choose **have they translated**. Read the complete sentence again 